],"truncated":false},"title":"6 todos","time":{"start":1782045944948,"end":1782045944950}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Go 1.26.4 available. Let me build a REST API for books using SQLite. I'll use the standard library net/http with a lightweight router (or just plain net/http with gorilla/mux). To keep dependencies minimal but practical, I'll use:\n- `github.com/mattn/go-sqlite3` for SQLite (requires CGO)\n- `github.com/gorilla/mux` for routing\n\nActually, to avoid CGO complications, let me consider using a pure-Go SQLite driver like `modernc.org/sqlite`. This avoids CGO entirely and is more portable.\n\nLet me plan the structure:\n- main.go - entry point, starts server\n- db.go - database init and helpers\n- handlers.go - HTTP handlers\n- models.go - Book struct\n- go.mod\n- README.md\n- *_test.go - tests\n\nI'll use modernc.org/sqlite (pure Go, no CGO). And gorilla/mux for routing (well-maintained, popular).\n\nLet me create the project.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eea3729090019RCdjUwqrXgWc6","sessionID":"ses_115c93e67ffeFqZgeAH4FYd0MW","messageID":"msg_eea36f79b001hxHADNIc4ntByC"}}
