{"type":"text","timestamp":1782046361595,"sessionID":"ses_115c93e67ffeFqZgeAH4FYd0MW","part":{"id":"prt_eea3d7b9e001fNpicZzXll9OHX","messageID":"msg_eea3d76870013rQM6hCAcl5GtV","sessionID":"ses_115c93e67ffeFqZgeAH4FYd0MW","type":"text","text":"Done. Built a Go book-collection REST API per TASK.md.\n\n**Files** (all in the workspace root):\n- `main.go` — entrypoint with flags `-addr` and `-db`, graceful shutdown\n- `models.go` — `Book` type, `bookInput` payload, strict (create) + partial (update) validation\n- `db.go` — `Store` wrapping `modernc.org/sqlite` (pure-Go, no CGO); schema + CRUD + author-filtered list\n- `handlers.go` — gorilla/mux router exposing `/health` and `/books` CRUD endpoints\n- `main_test.go` — 8 test functions (6 unit + 3 integration, well over the 3-test minimum)\n- `go.mod` / `go.sum` — module `bookapi` with `github.com/gorilla/mux` and `modernc.org/sqlite`\n- `README.md` — setup, run, endpoint reference, example session\n\n**Verification:**\n- `go vet ./...` clean\n- `go build ./...` clean\n- `go test ./...` — `ok bookapi` (all 8 tests pass)\n- Smoke-tested the built binary against a real port: `health`, create (201), list, `?author=` filter, get, partial PUT, 404/400/422/400 error paths, and delete (204 → 404) all behaved correctly","time":{"start":1782046358430,"end":1782046361590}}}
